l Murphy, powered by Colony Spark [https://www.colonyspark.com/]=0A=0A=C2=
=A0=0A=0AOctober 2, 2026=0A=0AA new look for The Operations Brief=0A=0AWe r=
efreshed the design to match our new website, so the newsletter and the sit=
e=0Anow read as one publication. What you get from it hasn=E2=80=99t change=
d: three sections=0Aevery week, written for the people running manufacturin=
g and distribution=0Aoperations. Thanks for reading.=0A=0AA warning from a =
machine, supplier, or quality team is not yet a customer=0Adecision. The us=
eful question is whether it touches an open order, how certain=0Athe warnin=
g is, and who can verify the next step before the promise changes.=0A=0AThi=
s issue is about that gap: why a list of alerts isn=E2=80=99t the same as a=
 review,=0Awhat a late order looks like from the floor, and a practical way=
 to check=0Awarnings against the orders you=E2=80=99ve already promised.=0A=
=0AThis week=E2=80=99s question=0A=0AWhat would help you act sooner on an a=
t-risk order=3F=0A=0ASee affected orders=0A[https://tally.so/r/pb8poB=3Fans=
wer=3DSee%20affected%20orders&email=3D${email}&campaign=3Dtob_poll_1&v=3D1]=
=0A=0AConfirm the facts=0A[https://tally.so/r/pb8poB=3Fanswer=3DConfirm%20t=
